SUMMARY:🚀 SpaceX｜Dragonfly（暂定）
LOCATION:Launch Complex 39A / Kennedy Space Center\, FL\, USA
DESCRIPTION:运载器：Falcon Heavy\n状态：To Be Determined\n时间精度：Day\n任务：Dragonfly
  is NASA's 4th New Frontiers program mission that will send a robotic ro
 torcraft to fly within the atmosphere of Saturn's moon Titan to sample m
 aterials and determine surface composition in different geologic setting
 s\, advancing humanity's search for the building blocks of life.\n\nThe 
 craft is a large quadcopter with double rotors with mass of about 875 kg
 \, featuring rotors of 1.35 m in diameter. It can fly through several ki
 lometers within an hour and will perform 1 flight per Titan day (~16 Ear
 th days). During the planned 3.3-year mission\, Dragonfly is expected to
  cover distance up to several hundred km.\n\nDragonfly will use a Multi-
 Mission Radioisotope Thermoelectric Generator (MMRTG) to power its instr
 uments.\n\nThe planned science instrument suite is:\n* DragonCam: Camera
  Suite\n* DrACO: Drill for Acquisition of Complex Organics\n* DraMS: Mas
 s Spectrometer\n* DraGNS: Gamma-ray and Neutron Spectrometer\n* DraGMet:
  Geophysics and Meteorology\n发射窗口（UTC）：2028-07-05T00:00:00Z – 2028-07-05
 T00:00:00Z\n数据源：Launch Library 2 / The Space Devs\n详情：https://ll.thespac
